        ],
        "support": "strong",
        "text": "The linked accuracy evidence supports the claim that Ansor's learned cost model was useful for ranking candidates in the reported ResNet-50 tuning experiment on Intel CPU: it used 20,000 measured programs for training and 5,000 for testing, with 0.079 RMSE, 0.958 R2, 0.851 pairwise comparison accuracy, and 0.624 recall@30."
      },
      {
        "claim_ids": [
          "claim-sampling-complete-programs-and-then-fine-tuning-them-with-evolutionary-search-an--98bcfa809814"
        ],
        "evidence_ids": [
